# Sprint 12 – Incident Response & Portfolio Completion

## Completed

- Performed a complete end-to-end incident response exercise within the enterprise lab environment.
- Verified Splunk Enterprise was receiving Windows, Sysmon, and PowerShell telemetry from domain systems.
- Captured pre-incident snapshots of all virtual machines.
- Generated controlled security events for investigation, including:
  - PowerShell execution
  - Windows Command Prompt execution
  - Certutil execution
  - Active Directory account creation
  - Local Administrator group modification
- Investigated security events using Splunk Enterprise.
- Correlated Windows Security, Sysmon, and PowerShell logs into a unified investigation timeline.
- Collected and documented evidence supporting the simulated incident.
- Assigned incident severity using a structured triage methodology.
- Performed containment by removing privileged access from the temporary account.
- Performed remediation by deleting the temporary Active Directory account and cleaning up test artifacts.
- Validated successful remediation and confirmed continued log ingestion.
- Completed technical and executive incident documentation.
- Finalized project architecture documentation.
- Organized the GitHub repository into professional documentation sections.
- Prepared the project for public portfolio presentation.

